WEBVTT

00:00:04.480 --> 00:00:05.850
Morning!

00:00:05.850 --> 00:00:07.050
Good morning!

00:00:07.050 --> 00:00:08.720
Morning, Hizume.

00:00:08.720 --> 00:00:10.990
Uki-san, good morning.

00:00:10.990 --> 00:00:12.990
Our performance yesterday was so much fun!

00:00:12.990 --> 00:00:16.440
Yes. My brother saw the footage 
of it that Sensei shot for us

00:00:16.440 --> 00:00:18.780
and regretted not going.

00:00:18.780 --> 00:00:20.820
<i>I see her brother hasn't changed...</i>

00:00:22.420 --> 00:00:23.620
What's the matter?

00:00:23.950 --> 00:00:27.180
Uh... Maybe I just imagined it...

00:00:37.140 --> 00:00:41.020
<b>Anima Yell!</b>

00:01:58.010 --> 00:02:00.680
<b>A/V Room</b>

00:02:04.560 --> 00:02:07.430
<i>Huh? The club room's open?</i>

00:02:08.130 --> 00:02:09.430
Is someone here?

00:02:11.360 --> 00:02:13.000
I guess someone <i>is</i> here, but...

00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:14.730
Wh-What's wrong, Kotetsu?

00:02:15.080 --> 00:02:17.850
I'm such a piggy bastard!

00:02:17.850 --> 00:02:19.470
Seriously, what happened?!

00:02:19.470 --> 00:02:22.120
Don't say stuff like that with such a cute face!

00:02:22.370 --> 00:02:26.370
<b>Episode 7: The One on Top Is Scared of Heights</b>

00:02:25.080 --> 00:02:26.370
I see.

00:02:26.730 --> 00:02:30.170
You didn't know that Kohane 
was scared of heights...

00:02:30.170 --> 00:02:32.130
I guess we never told you.

00:02:32.440 --> 00:02:34.560
I feel so ashamed.

00:02:34.560 --> 00:02:36.090
Ashamed?

00:02:36.540 --> 00:02:40.360
Kohane-chan's scared of heights, 
but she still went up top...

00:02:40.360 --> 00:02:44.720
And yet I declined for a stupid reason 
like worrying about how heavy I was.

00:02:45.210 --> 00:02:46.990
I'm a pig, inside and out!

00:02:46.990 --> 00:02:49.500
My name might mean "tiger," 
but I'm a tiger from the family Suidae!

00:02:47.730 --> 00:02:51.980
Pigs belong to the family Suidae

00:02:49.230 --> 00:02:51.980
Tigers belong to the family Felidae

00:02:49.500 --> 00:02:51.980
Calm down! You aren't making any sense!

00:02:52.360 --> 00:02:56.360
I thought the least I could do was exercise 
more so my body wouldn't be so piggish!

00:02:57.430 --> 00:02:59.660
I heard everything.

00:03:00.110 --> 00:03:01.640
You scared me...

00:03:01.640 --> 00:03:05.240
But I don't think you're fat, Kotetsu-san.

00:03:05.830 --> 00:03:06.680
See?

00:03:07.730 --> 00:03:09.950
U-Um... That might be the case for you,

00:03:09.950 --> 00:03:13.310
since you've gone through 
special training, but...

00:03:13.310 --> 00:03:14.670
Special training?

00:03:15.240 --> 00:03:16.670
A-Anyway,

00:03:17.200 --> 00:03:21.550
I want to save Kohane-chan 
from that dire situation.

00:03:21.550 --> 00:03:26.760
By "dire," does she mean the 
double base thigh stand?

00:03:26.760 --> 00:03:28.060
I-I think so?

00:03:36.690 --> 00:03:39.790
Kohane-chan! Kohane-chan's 
flying through the sky!

00:03:39.790 --> 00:03:41.150
What the heck did you show her?!

00:03:42.750 --> 00:03:44.280
What's all this stuff?

00:03:44.280 --> 00:03:47.670
I brought all the workout and 
diet stuff I found at home!

00:03:48.940 --> 00:03:52.920
I don't think any of this 
will be very effective...

00:03:52.920 --> 00:03:56.140
Really?! As an expert, you don't 
think any of those will work?

00:03:56.140 --> 00:03:57.670
An expert in what?

00:03:58.040 --> 00:04:02.520
I mean... I think the fact that you're 
not satisfied with your weight

00:04:02.520 --> 00:04:04.430
is proof enough...

00:04:05.560 --> 00:04:09.000
N-No, it's just that I'm not strong-willed!

00:04:09.000 --> 00:04:10.760
They did nothing wrong!

00:04:10.760 --> 00:04:12.060
Why are you defending them?

00:04:12.530 --> 00:04:14.600
If you're not strong-willed,

00:04:14.600 --> 00:04:17.690
maybe we just need to give you an 
incentive so you don't lose hope easily.

00:04:18.000 --> 00:04:19.130
Like what?

00:04:19.130 --> 00:04:20.400
Well...

00:04:21.030 --> 00:04:24.520
If you haven't lost any weight in a week...

00:04:25.350 --> 00:04:28.030
No more bringing snacks into the club room,

00:04:28.030 --> 00:04:29.180
or something...

00:04:30.530 --> 00:04:32.130
Where did Kotetsu-san go?

00:04:32.130 --> 00:04:35.100
She turned pale and bolted out of the room.

00:04:41.360 --> 00:04:42.590
But Kotetsu-san,

00:04:43.200 --> 00:04:46.180
I'm noticing that you seem 
more fatigued than usual.

00:04:46.180 --> 00:04:48.100
N-No, not at all...

00:04:49.980 --> 00:04:51.720
Did you happen to skip breakfast?

00:04:52.180 --> 00:04:55.190
I ate breakfast! I ate lots!

00:04:56.720 --> 00:04:58.690
Your body doesn't lie.

00:04:58.690 --> 00:05:07.530
<b>Chocolate Coronet</b>

00:04:58.690 --> 00:05:07.530
New

00:04:58.690 --> 00:05:07.530
Roll (Peanut Cream)

00:04:59.460 --> 00:05:01.790
You shouldn't force yourself not to eat.

00:05:01.790 --> 00:05:03.060
Here, have some of these.

00:05:04.120 --> 00:05:05.390
I'm sorry.

00:05:05.390 --> 00:05:07.530
I guess you need a forced break.

00:05:07.880 --> 00:05:11.840
Come to think of it, why is 
Kohane-san scared of heights?

00:05:11.840 --> 00:05:13.720
Now that you mention it...

00:05:13.720 --> 00:05:16.370
She wasn't always scared of them.

00:05:18.120 --> 00:05:20.520
I wonder why...

00:05:24.360 --> 00:05:26.840
<i>I'm so distracted by how 
fast Kotetsu is eating,</i>

00:05:26.840 --> 00:05:28.800
<i>I can't even gather my thoughts!</i>

00:05:29.150 --> 00:05:31.640
Oh, that's right! She fell and got hurt.

00:05:32.160 --> 00:05:35.230
Her parents even came from work to get her.

00:05:35.230 --> 00:05:39.060
So that memory must have caused her fear.

00:05:39.060 --> 00:05:40.820
I think so, but...

00:05:40.820 --> 00:05:43.260
Oh, everyone's here already.

00:05:44.280 --> 00:05:45.920
You're having snacks?

00:05:45.920 --> 00:05:46.990
I'm on a diet.

00:05:46.990 --> 00:05:49.260
By stuffing your face with snacks?

00:05:51.460 --> 00:05:53.580
The reason I'm scared of heights?

00:05:53.580 --> 00:05:55.950
You fell and got hurt, right?

00:05:56.560 --> 00:06:00.300
Oh, that's right. I think the wind 
was really strong that day...

00:06:04.170 --> 00:06:06.360
The wind's so strong.

00:06:07.570 --> 00:06:08.790
That means...

00:06:09.180 --> 00:06:10.460
I can fly!

00:06:10.460 --> 00:06:11.980
I actually did fly a little bit.

00:06:11.980 --> 00:06:13.310
That's called "falling"!

00:06:16.470 --> 00:06:18.520
When I woke up, I was in the hospital,

00:06:19.520 --> 00:06:23.980
and I was surrounded by my mom, 
my dad, and my friends.

00:06:23.980 --> 00:06:27.180
Hey, listen to this! I flew through the—

00:06:28.520 --> 00:06:29.910
Thank goodness...

00:06:30.320 --> 00:06:32.440
You dummy.

00:06:34.370 --> 00:06:37.280
I-I was so scared!

00:06:37.280 --> 00:06:39.040
K-Kohane-chan...

00:06:39.040 --> 00:06:40.890
Everyone was crying.

00:06:41.620 --> 00:06:47.050
I realized that it was my fault,
that I had made them all cry and feel sad.

00:06:48.680 --> 00:06:52.050
Ever since then, I've been scared 
of high places in general.

00:06:54.810 --> 00:06:56.620
I'm such a pig!

00:06:56.620 --> 00:06:59.210
I'm just going to oink from now on!

00:06:59.210 --> 00:07:02.940
Uh, I didn't talk about you or any pigs...

00:07:02.940 --> 00:07:04.680
I wouldn't say I'm moved,

00:07:04.680 --> 00:07:07.700
but I definitely feel for your parents.

00:07:08.160 --> 00:07:11.280
That reminds me... You did actually 
jump out of a tree at me.

00:07:11.610 --> 00:07:15.200
Yeah... I'm so surprised you 
actually managed to grow so big.

00:07:15.480 --> 00:07:16.780
Big...

00:07:17.840 --> 00:07:19.230
Big?

00:07:19.230 --> 00:07:20.210
Uki?

00:07:20.490 --> 00:07:24.020
You don't have to push yourself 
if you don't like high places!

00:07:24.680 --> 00:07:29.420
I mean, not immediately, 
but I'll get lighter...

00:07:29.420 --> 00:07:32.300
Um, this... This is...

00:07:32.300 --> 00:07:34.460
This is my last one!

00:07:35.460 --> 00:07:37.560
<i>She's not gonna get any lighter.</i>

00:07:38.370 --> 00:07:41.810
Thanks, Kotecchan! But I'll 
be the one who goes on top!

00:07:42.480 --> 00:07:46.190
Besides, I'm more used to high 
places than I was before!

00:07:47.160 --> 00:07:48.330
Look!

00:07:48.330 --> 00:07:50.440
That's no different from before.

00:07:50.730 --> 00:07:51.800
But look!

00:07:53.710 --> 00:07:56.860
I guess Kohane and Kotetsu are 
basically in the same boat.

00:07:56.860 --> 00:07:58.270
D'oh...

00:07:58.270 --> 00:08:00.890
But if Kohane-san is willing to be on top,

00:08:00.890 --> 00:08:03.630
doesn't that make Kotetsu-san's diet pointless?

00:08:03.630 --> 00:08:04.960
Oh, right.

00:08:04.960 --> 00:08:09.210
Actually, if you got bigger, you 
might even be a sturdier base!

00:08:09.640 --> 00:08:11.340
I'm losing weight, no matter what!

00:08:11.830 --> 00:08:16.060
Just because someone is bigger doesn't 
guarantee they'll be a good base.

00:08:16.060 --> 00:08:19.100
G-Got it. You're really close, Hizume.

00:08:19.100 --> 00:08:22.940
For now, I think we can keep moving 
forward with our current positions.

00:08:22.940 --> 00:08:23.810
Right.

00:08:24.190 --> 00:08:25.520
I'll be on top!

00:08:25.990 --> 00:08:28.110
Hizume and Kotecchan will be the bases,

00:08:28.440 --> 00:08:31.670
and Uki's, um... The s...

00:08:32.410 --> 00:08:33.450
straightman!

00:08:33.450 --> 00:08:35.120
I guess you at least got the "S" right?!

00:08:33.530 --> 00:08:35.030
Spotter

00:08:35.120 --> 00:08:37.470
But maybe I'll finally be able to fly now!

00:08:37.470 --> 00:08:39.120
What are you even talking about?

00:08:39.120 --> 00:08:42.720
K-Kohane-chan, let's not...

00:08:42.720 --> 00:08:46.250
I mean, uh, if you happened 
to hit your head again...

00:08:46.840 --> 00:08:50.000
I get the feeling you're thinking 
something pretty awful.

00:08:50.380 --> 00:08:52.510
I can do it as long as I have you guys!

00:08:52.800 --> 00:08:55.180
I know you guys will support me!

00:08:57.460 --> 00:08:59.610
Right...

00:09:00.070 --> 00:09:04.220
Then let's go one step further 
today and try a shoulder straddle.

00:09:04.220 --> 00:09:06.190
What kind of technique is that?

00:09:06.190 --> 00:09:08.270
Essentially, you sit on someone's shoulders.

00:09:08.270 --> 00:09:09.610
Bring it on!

00:09:12.430 --> 00:09:14.510
Looks like we acted too soon...

00:09:14.510 --> 00:09:16.640
You okay, Kohane?

00:09:16.640 --> 00:09:18.120
Kohane-chan...

00:09:18.690 --> 00:09:22.360
It's okay! I'll be able to do it soon!

00:09:22.360 --> 00:09:23.620
With a smile!

00:09:23.620 --> 00:09:26.550
Seriously, where does your 
confidence come from?

00:09:39.680 --> 00:09:43.540
Kohane, you've gotten really 
good at making pom poms.

00:09:43.540 --> 00:09:45.420
Well, I've made lots, you know.

00:09:46.520 --> 00:09:48.740
Really? Lots?

00:09:49.770 --> 00:09:51.770
What are we supposed to do with all these?!

00:09:51.770 --> 00:09:53.590
I-I just couldn't stop.

00:09:54.660 --> 00:09:58.490
Maybe we can hand them out to 
kids in our class, like Kon-chan.

00:09:58.490 --> 00:10:00.670
Even though they're not cheerleading?

00:10:00.670 --> 00:10:03.400
You don't have to be a 
cheerleader to use pom poms!

00:10:03.400 --> 00:10:04.160
Huh?

00:10:04.160 --> 00:10:08.120
They work as hair ribbons, 
key holders, house decorations...

00:10:08.660 --> 00:10:09.720
and even wigs!

00:10:09.720 --> 00:10:11.000
Funky!

00:10:11.320 --> 00:10:13.590
Oh, hey... We're out of ribbon.

00:10:13.590 --> 00:10:16.440
Jeez... You made way too many.

00:10:16.440 --> 00:10:18.340
Where do they sell that ribbon?

00:10:18.620 --> 00:10:23.040
I had my mom buy some online.

00:10:23.040 --> 00:10:24.100
Ah...

00:10:24.790 --> 00:10:27.640
Shall we go buy some at the cheer shop?

00:10:30.440 --> 00:10:35.240
Ch-Ch-Ch-Cheer shop?
 What kind of shop is that?

00:10:35.240 --> 00:10:38.040
As the name suggests, it's a shop 
specializing in cheerleading supplies.

00:10:38.040 --> 00:10:41.110
They sell cheer uniforms 
and other useful things.

00:10:41.110 --> 00:10:45.410
I see. So you can actually buy stuff 
at a shop and not just online.

00:10:45.540 --> 00:10:50.420
<b>Cheer Shop</b>

00:10:46.240 --> 00:10:50.420
To think that such a heavenly 
paradise exists...

00:10:50.870 --> 00:10:53.150
She's definitely imagining 
something that doesn't exist.

00:10:53.150 --> 00:10:56.730
But I'd like to go to the cheer shop, too.

00:10:56.730 --> 00:10:58.480
Me too, too, too, too, too!

00:10:58.480 --> 00:11:01.360
Well, tomorrow is Saturday,

00:11:01.360 --> 00:11:04.270
so why don't we all go to 
the cheer shop together?

00:11:04.270 --> 00:11:06.700
Yeah! Yay!

00:11:06.700 --> 00:11:09.560
<i>Well, tomorrow's going to be a rough day.</i>

00:11:06.700 --> 00:11:10.280
Cheer shop! Cheer shop!

00:11:23.140 --> 00:11:26.280
Sorry to keep you waiting. 
Am I the last one here?

00:11:26.280 --> 00:11:28.040
Good... morning?!

00:11:28.400 --> 00:11:30.260
What's going on?!

00:11:30.660 --> 00:11:34.060
She's so worked up, I'm afraid
she's gonna wear herself out.

00:11:34.060 --> 00:11:35.420
I-I see.

00:11:35.420 --> 00:11:37.530
I mean, we're going to the cheer shop!

00:11:37.530 --> 00:11:40.200
A cheer shop! A shop for cheerleading!

00:11:40.200 --> 00:11:42.110
We know! Calm down!

00:11:42.110 --> 00:11:44.270
Jeez, where's all this strength coming from?

00:11:43.720 --> 00:11:49.270
<b>Yon Drugs</b>

00:11:44.270 --> 00:11:46.970
They should be opening up
at any moment. Let's go.

00:11:46.970 --> 00:11:48.470
Yeah!

00:11:51.200 --> 00:11:53.100
This is the cheer shop.

00:11:59.280 --> 00:12:01.270
Wow!

00:12:02.360 --> 00:12:03.990
It's so cute!

00:12:06.310 --> 00:12:10.600
So... So this is heaven! The cheer shop!

00:12:10.600 --> 00:12:11.750
You're soaked with sweat.

00:12:12.660 --> 00:12:14.000
Welcome.

00:12:14.000 --> 00:12:15.250
She's superb!

00:12:15.250 --> 00:12:18.220
I-I'm not a supervisor...

00:12:18.220 --> 00:12:20.010
Oh, don't mind her.

00:12:20.330 --> 00:12:23.560
I've been a regular at this shop 
since I was in middle school.

00:12:23.560 --> 00:12:25.480
Wait, is that Senpai?! Why?!

00:12:25.480 --> 00:12:27.610
Here are some training uniforms.

00:12:27.610 --> 00:12:29.080
Wow!

00:12:30.410 --> 00:12:33.280
The hair ribbons and 
accessories are this way.

00:12:33.280 --> 00:12:34.810
Ooh, where? Where?!

00:12:36.020 --> 00:12:38.020
Thank you very much.

00:12:38.380 --> 00:12:40.490
Wow, they're so cute!

00:12:40.490 --> 00:12:42.720
And there are so many designs!

00:12:42.720 --> 00:12:43.600
Right?

00:12:43.600 --> 00:12:44.760
Uki?

00:12:44.760 --> 00:12:47.950
Uh... My eyes suddenly feel really tired.

00:12:47.950 --> 00:12:50.120
All these primary colors 
are making me see stars.

00:12:50.120 --> 00:12:52.620
Wow, they even have uniforms!

00:12:53.240 --> 00:12:54.920
You can try them on, if you'd like.

00:12:55.380 --> 00:12:57.740
Uki! Let's try some on!

00:12:57.740 --> 00:13:01.320
Huh?! Well... I guess I don't mind these.

00:13:03.260 --> 00:13:05.690
Okay! Let's try these on!

00:13:05.690 --> 00:13:06.760
Hang on a second!

00:13:10.000 --> 00:13:12.770
You two look so cute!

00:13:14.890 --> 00:13:16.770
Perfect!

00:13:18.230 --> 00:13:20.770
The ones with the shorts 
are super cute, too!

00:13:20.770 --> 00:13:23.200
Aren't you two going to try any on?

00:13:23.200 --> 00:13:25.780
Oh, I'm way too busy for that.

00:13:26.190 --> 00:13:27.630
So this is how its sewn here.

00:13:27.630 --> 00:13:29.780
<i>Oh... She's planning to make one herself.</i>

00:13:30.200 --> 00:13:33.660
Wow, they even have shoes and bags!

00:13:33.660 --> 00:13:37.040
And lapel pins and hats, too.

00:13:37.040 --> 00:13:40.570
They look really cool, but I don't 
think I could use them at school.

00:13:40.570 --> 00:13:43.880
That's not true! It's totally fine!

00:13:44.320 --> 00:13:46.680
Actually, you could even 
decorate your uniform!

00:13:46.990 --> 00:13:48.400
Morning!

00:13:48.400 --> 00:13:49.930
Morning.

00:13:49.930 --> 00:13:51.850
I have to do that with you?

00:13:51.850 --> 00:13:54.100
They have catalogs over here.

00:13:54.560 --> 00:13:56.430
Ooh, let's see, let's see, let's see.

00:13:56.430 --> 00:14:00.310
<b><i>Metallic Pom Poms</i></b>

00:13:56.760 --> 00:14:00.310
Ooh! They have so many cute things!

00:14:00.310 --> 00:14:01.690
<b>Uniform (top and bottom)</b>

00:14:02.110 --> 00:14:03.480
<b>Metallic Pom Poms</b>

00:14:05.990 --> 00:14:10.420
Please... At least let me dream a little!

00:14:11.510 --> 00:14:13.240
<i>Maybe that just gave her false hope.</i>

00:14:13.890 --> 00:14:17.500
We came here today for 
pom pom ribbon, remember?

00:14:19.170 --> 00:14:22.280
But there are so many, I can't decide!

00:14:22.280 --> 00:14:25.260
You can make some nice 
ones by mixing colors, too.

00:14:25.260 --> 00:14:26.820
Like these two.

00:14:28.280 --> 00:14:32.870
You can do three colors, and 
even try using different materials.

00:14:32.870 --> 00:14:36.020
Wow... I want them all!

00:14:36.680 --> 00:14:40.030
Let's buy them all and pretend 
we actually have club funds!

00:14:40.030 --> 00:14:43.020
Hey, using money you don't 
have isn't an option!

00:14:47.540 --> 00:14:49.530
It was a place filled with dreams.

00:14:50.210 --> 00:14:53.680
But now we can accept cheer 
requests at any time!

00:14:53.680 --> 00:14:55.160
We can make plenty!

00:14:55.490 --> 00:15:00.120
In that case, may I put in a request?

00:15:01.200 --> 00:15:02.920
We don't need any pom poms.

00:15:03.990 --> 00:15:07.310
It's actually more of a 
discussion than a request.

00:15:07.310 --> 00:15:10.510
Oh, come on. You don't have 
to put in a request for that.

00:15:10.510 --> 00:15:11.970
We're happy to listen any time.

00:15:12.320 --> 00:15:16.360
<i>Is this actually why she 
invited us to go out shopping?</i>

00:15:16.800 --> 00:15:19.100
<i>Will we be able to help her out?</i>

00:15:19.100 --> 00:15:24.170
<i>W-Would someone like me be able 
to offer Hizume-chan any advice?</i>

00:15:24.170 --> 00:15:26.110
<i>Is it about cheerleading?</i>

00:15:26.110 --> 00:15:28.500
<i>Something's troubling Hizume?</i>

00:15:29.880 --> 00:15:31.610
<i>Ooh, this is yummy.</i>

00:15:31.610 --> 00:15:34.650
You see, I'm having a hard 
time fitting in with my class.

00:15:34.650 --> 00:15:37.120
They don't seem to think very highly of me.

00:15:37.440 --> 00:15:38.440
What?!

00:15:38.440 --> 00:15:39.870
Yeah, what the heck?!

00:15:40.280 --> 00:15:43.560
It's been two months 
since the new term started!

00:15:43.560 --> 00:15:46.420
You've been alone this 
whole time? That's so sad!

00:15:46.420 --> 00:15:48.960
Yes... You're right...

00:15:48.960 --> 00:15:51.580
Kotetsu! Put those daggers away!

00:15:51.580 --> 00:15:53.300
I'm so sorry!

00:15:53.780 --> 00:15:57.240
But maybe it's not as negative as you think.

00:15:57.240 --> 00:15:59.240
You might just be worrying too much.

00:15:59.240 --> 00:16:00.200
No!

00:16:01.180 --> 00:16:04.190
First of all, everyone's avoiding me.

00:16:04.820 --> 00:16:08.330
The other day, I was caught 
in a sudden downpour,

00:16:08.330 --> 00:16:12.030
but everyone was just showing 
off their umbrellas.

00:16:12.640 --> 00:16:15.530
They avoid me during PE, as well.

00:16:18.570 --> 00:16:22.090
But if they're avoiding you in class...

00:16:23.090 --> 00:16:25.600
Arima-san's so lovely...

00:16:25.600 --> 00:16:27.290
She has such an aura.

00:16:27.290 --> 00:16:29.690
Showing off their umbrellas...

00:16:29.690 --> 00:16:32.810
Wh-Why don't we try to ask her if 
she'd like to walk home with us?

00:16:32.810 --> 00:16:35.180
But we'd just be annoying her.

00:16:35.600 --> 00:16:37.770
And they avoid you during PE...

00:16:37.770 --> 00:16:40.570
I'm so embarrassed to exercise with Arima-san!

00:16:40.570 --> 00:16:43.080
I want to stretch with Arima-san sometime...

00:16:43.080 --> 00:16:45.100
Hey, no headstarts!

00:16:45.440 --> 00:16:47.100
Isn't that what all that means?

00:16:47.100 --> 00:16:49.850
You're entirely too positive, Kohane-san!

00:16:49.850 --> 00:16:52.560
Actually, I don't think she's wrong.

00:16:52.560 --> 00:16:53.700
Not you, too, Uki-san!

00:16:54.310 --> 00:16:59.360
You look like the calm and quiet type, 
so you might seem hard to talk to.

00:16:59.360 --> 00:17:01.080
Yeah, I think so, too.

00:17:01.480 --> 00:17:04.580
You might be more approachable if you 
smile like you do when performing.

00:17:04.580 --> 00:17:07.230
Yeah, I totally agree!

00:17:07.230 --> 00:17:09.840
What's up, Kotetsu? You're never this loud!

00:17:10.280 --> 00:17:11.620
<i>Senpai...</i>

00:17:15.090 --> 00:17:18.330
This'll be quickly solved if you 
can be more approachable.

00:17:18.330 --> 00:17:19.970
It can't be that easy.

00:17:19.970 --> 00:17:22.730
Hey, why not hand out pom poms?

00:17:22.730 --> 00:17:24.800
You can introduce yourself 
<i>and</i> recruit people.

00:17:24.800 --> 00:17:26.100
Two birds with one stone!

00:17:26.660 --> 00:17:28.860
Please, take one!

00:17:30.850 --> 00:17:33.130
Am I running for office?

00:17:33.130 --> 00:17:34.360
<i>Pretty much...</i>

00:17:34.800 --> 00:17:38.560
But I guess I'll never know if I don't try.

00:17:38.560 --> 00:17:39.620
Yeah!

00:17:40.040 --> 00:17:42.960
Please retrieve my bones if I die...

00:17:42.960 --> 00:17:46.120
You look like a soldier who's about 
to go off to battle, Hizume.

00:17:46.120 --> 00:17:49.130
You might actually end up super popular!

00:17:49.130 --> 00:17:50.760
Super popular?

00:17:52.120 --> 00:17:54.380
<i>I think that's beyond her 
imagination's limits.</i>

00:18:10.920 --> 00:18:12.680
They're avoiding her.

00:18:15.490 --> 00:18:17.880
Was the change too much, too fast?

00:18:17.880 --> 00:18:19.910
She even wore her uniform.

00:18:20.170 --> 00:18:21.690
Senpai...

00:18:23.330 --> 00:18:26.430
Um... What are you doing, Arima-san?

00:18:26.430 --> 00:18:28.790
Are you... okay?

00:18:28.790 --> 00:18:30.040
Don't!

00:18:30.040 --> 00:18:32.170
Wo... rry!

00:18:33.750 --> 00:18:35.800
O-Okay...

00:18:35.800 --> 00:18:38.970
You don't need to talk in cheers, Hizume!

00:18:51.300 --> 00:18:52.470
High V!

00:18:53.240 --> 00:18:54.860
Low V!

00:18:55.240 --> 00:18:58.380
I know that silence was painful, 
but that's not helping!

00:18:58.380 --> 00:19:02.600
People backed off when Kohane-chan 
and I tried that, too...

00:19:07.300 --> 00:19:09.260
They're moving even further away.

00:19:09.260 --> 00:19:11.860
Won't someone try to get closer?

00:19:14.320 --> 00:19:15.750
Hizume!

00:19:17.180 --> 00:19:20.260
I'll help you. You're my friend!

00:19:21.560 --> 00:19:22.600
No fair!

00:19:22.600 --> 00:19:25.360
No fair! Don't hog Arima-san!

00:19:25.360 --> 00:19:27.880
You're Hatoya-san from Class 2, aren't you?

00:19:27.880 --> 00:19:29.440
From the cheer association!

00:19:29.440 --> 00:19:32.770
Just because you're in the same association
doesn't mean you get to cling to her 24/7!

00:19:40.570 --> 00:19:42.280
See? It's just like we thought.

00:19:42.720 --> 00:19:46.370
Everyone was too nervous to talk to 
Hizume because they liked her so much.

00:19:46.700 --> 00:19:51.120
They all recognized that they had a common 
enemy and decided to work together.

00:19:51.120 --> 00:19:52.760
Can I have one, Arima-san?

00:19:52.760 --> 00:19:53.850
Me, too!

00:19:53.850 --> 00:19:55.370
I want two!

00:19:55.370 --> 00:19:56.570
Then I want three!

00:19:56.570 --> 00:19:58.380
I'll take this and cheer you on next time!

00:19:58.380 --> 00:20:00.650
Why am I the enemy?!

00:20:00.650 --> 00:20:04.490
Don't I get to be a Hizume fangirl, too?

00:20:04.490 --> 00:20:07.950
You're going to help make 
sure Hizume's happy, right?

00:20:07.950 --> 00:20:09.640
You call this helping?!

00:20:11.010 --> 00:20:11.950
Everyone.

00:20:11.950 --> 00:20:13.390
Oh, Hizume-chan.

00:20:13.740 --> 00:20:17.770
Thank you for all of your 
advice the other day.

00:20:18.550 --> 00:20:22.040
Now I'm surrounded by people.

00:20:22.040 --> 00:20:24.700
Though they're facing the wrong way...

00:20:24.700 --> 00:20:28.030
They're on guard to make sure no 
one bad tries to come near you.

00:20:28.460 --> 00:20:29.650
Boo.

00:20:29.650 --> 00:20:31.160
Fine, then!

00:20:31.160 --> 00:20:34.680
I'll just turn into the evil Tweetlebub.

00:20:31.730 --> 00:20:32.900
Tweet, tweet.

00:20:34.680 --> 00:20:37.170
What kind of weak-sounding character is that?

00:20:37.730 --> 00:20:40.910
Hey, it's the girls from the 
cheer association again!

00:20:40.910 --> 00:20:45.040
Arima-san, we're going to get some tea 
in the cafeteria. You should join us.

00:20:45.040 --> 00:20:48.520
I think I'll have whatever 
you have, Arima-san.

00:20:48.520 --> 00:20:50.560
B-But I have practice.

00:20:51.300 --> 00:20:53.520
Don't worry, Hizume-chan.

00:20:53.520 --> 00:20:55.810
We'll take our time getting there.

00:20:56.870 --> 00:20:59.420
Sorry, and thank you.

00:21:00.390 --> 00:21:02.120
I wanna go, too!

00:21:02.120 --> 00:21:03.950
Come on, we're going to the club room.

00:21:06.380 --> 00:21:10.120
What if Hizume gets recruited 
into another club?

00:21:10.120 --> 00:21:11.830
I see the roles have reversed.

00:21:12.280 --> 00:21:16.330
Usually it's Hizume who's always 
worried you're going to quit.

00:21:16.330 --> 00:21:18.030
Oh, really?

00:21:18.030 --> 00:21:21.750
I'm pretty sure Hizume-chan 
won't quit cheerleading.

00:21:18.330 --> 00:21:20.590
<b>A/V Room</b>

00:21:26.090 --> 00:21:28.850
<b>Curse</b>

00:21:29.320 --> 00:21:32.160
Wow! Who prepared this surprise
celebration for Hizume?

00:21:32.100 --> 00:21:37.350
<b>Celebration</b>

00:21:32.160 --> 00:21:34.100
Must be nice being so stupid!

00:21:34.600 --> 00:21:37.350
<b>Curse</b>

00:21:37.350 --> 00:21:40.110
<b>Curse</b>

00:21:37.730 --> 00:21:40.190
M-Maybe there really is a ghost?

00:21:40.190 --> 00:21:43.110
Uki-chan, ghosts don't use magic tape.

00:21:43.110 --> 00:21:45.740
So you've come, cheer association!

00:21:46.590 --> 00:21:48.490
You bunch of villains!

00:21:50.160 --> 00:21:51.900
Thank goodness. She's human.

00:21:51.900 --> 00:21:55.870
Hey, are you listening? 
Why do you seem so happy?

00:21:56.640 --> 00:22:00.000
Senpai's too good for this association!

00:22:00.000 --> 00:22:01.510
Senpai?

00:23:39.080 --> 00:23:41.480
Next time: "Senpai and Me."
